{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"BIT-libphp-2026-7258","published":"2026-05-12T08:50:25.509Z","modified":"2026-07-08T08:11:31.161434736Z","aliases":["BIT-php-2026-7258","BIT-php-min-2026-7258","CVE-2026-7258","GHSA-m8rr-4c36-8gq4"],"summary":"Out-of-bounds read in urldecode() on NetBSD","details":"In PHP versions 8.2.* before 8.2.31, 8.3.* before 8.3.31, 8.4.* before 8.4.21, and 8.5.* before 8.5.6, some functions, including urldecode(), pass signed char to ctype functions (like isxdigit()). On the systems with default signed char and optimized table-lookup ctype functions - such as NetBSD - this can lead to accessing array with negative offset, which can trigger a denial of service.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libphp","ecosystem":"Bitnami","purl":"pkg:bitnami/libphp"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"8.2.0"},{"fixed":"8.2.31"},{"introduced":"8.3.0"},{"fixed":"8.3.31"},{"introduced":"8.4.0"},{"fixed":"8.4.21"},{"introduced":"8.5.0"},{"fixed":"8.5.6"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/bitnami/vulndb/tree/main/data/libphp/BIT-libphp-2026-7258.json"},"severity":[{"type":"CVSS_V4","score":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:L/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:Amber"}]}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/security/advisories/GHSA-m8rr-4c36-8gq4"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-7258"}],"database_specific":{"cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:php:php:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"severity":"Medium"}}